    <user>anag_factory</user>
    <comment>Update qmqtt to 1.0.8.

Upstream 1.0.8 is a build/test-only release: it merges the three fixes this
package was carrying as patches (gh#emqx/qmqtt#269 tests built with the
library's SSL configuration, #270 the CMake test tree building against either
Qt major, #271 the CMake export installed once instead of twice). All three
patches are therefore dropped; the library sources themselves are unchanged,
so the ABI and the SONAMEs (libqmqtt-qt5.so.1, libqmqtt-qt6.so.1) stay put and
no rebuild of the one consumer (jaero) is needed.

The remaining downstream patch, qmqtt-flavoured-install-names.patch, is
rebased onto 1.0.8 (context only).

The spec also picks up a spec-cleaner-driven relocation of the
ExclusiveArch guard into the tag block; it produces identical RPMs, hence no
changelog bullet.

Built locally on aarch64 against openSUSE_Tumbleweed, both _multibuild
flavours green, 107 Google Test cases passing each. rpmlint unchanged from
the 1.0.7 baseline (1 error, 1 badness: invalid-spec-name, inherent to the
flavour split). source_validator clean.</comment>
